# Scratch-file patterns for FILES are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern
# with no slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore
# silently excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and a
# cold clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local check
# passed.
#
# Tool CACHE DIRECTORIES are the opposite case and are listed BOTH anchored and
# unanchored, because pytest, hypothesis and ruff write their caches into
# whatever directory they were invoked from. Running `python -m pytest .` from
# tests/ creates tests/.hypothesis/, which an anchored pattern alone does not
# cover; that directory then carries absolute build-machine paths in its
# constants files. No fixture in this repository is named after any of them, so
# matching them at any depth costs nothing.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
